cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FedGraph-RL: RL-orchestrated federated GNN fraud detection"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Gaurav
    family-names: Kosare
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-30
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/GauravKosare/fedgraph-rl"
abstract: >
  A NumPy-only research sandbox that combines a graph neural network fraud
  detector, federated learning across simulated non-IID edge devices, and a
  reinforcement-learning controller for per-round client selection and
  compute-budget allocation. A 5-seed evaluation finds that the learned
  controller reliably beats a fixed training cohort but ties uniform-random
  client selection and a fraud-rate heuristic — a reproducible null result
  consistent with the federated-learning literature.
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - graph neural network
  - reinforcement learning
  - client selection
  - fraud detection
